Sval: An open Favorite's switch-to-tab row wears the star

A Favorite's page that is open in a tab is offered as a switch-to-tab row,
which `UrlbarView` draws as `type="switchtab"` whatever the result's source,
so the star its other rows wear (`favorites-history-rows.patch`) is lost.
Favorites are not in Places, so no provider can say the page is one, and no
API marks another component's row. The view marks the row from
`SvalFavoritesProvider.nameOf`, and Sval's stylesheet draws the star.

